==Middle English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|enm|dett|det}}
* {{q|rare}} {{alter|enm|debte|deatte|debt}}

===Etymology===
From {{bor|enm|fro|dete}}, from {{der|enm|ML.|dēbita}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|lang=enm|/ˈdɛt(ə)/}}

===Noun===
{{enm-noun|dettes }}

# [[goods|Goods]] or [[possessions]] owed to or due to another person; a [[debt]].
# The state of debt; the condition one is when one has a debt or monetary obligation.
# Something which one is [[obliged]] to do {{gloss|by law, society, or belief}}:
## [[sex|Sex]] {{gloss|i.e. as something which one's partner requires of oneself}}.
## [[death|Death]] {{gloss|i.e. as something which the nature of humanity requires of oneself}}
## {{lb|enm|rare}} The requirement to fight back against one who has hurt oneself.
# Something that one [[deserves]] (negatively); one's fate or [[punishment]].
# {{lb|enm|theology}} [[sin|Sin]]; acts which go against the dictates of a higher power.
#*:{{quote-book|year=a.1382|author=John Wycliffe|title={{w|Wycliffe's Bible}} |chapter=Matheu 6:9-14|passage=And thus ye ſchulen preye, Oure fadir that art in heuenes, halewid be thi name; / thi kyngdoom come to; be thi wille don `in erthe as in heuene; / ȝyue to vs this dai oure `breed ouer othir ſubſtaunce; / and forȝyue to vs oure '''dettis''', as we forȝyuen to oure dettouris; and lede vs not in to temptacioun, / but delyuere vs fro yuel / Amen {{...}}|translation=And you should pray like this: "Our father that's in heaven, your name will be hailed; / your kingdom will come; your will will be done on Earth just like in heaven; / give us our bread or other sustenance today; / and forgive us of our '''sins''', as we forgive those who sin against us; and don't let us fall into temptation, but instead save us from evil. / Amen." {{...}}|lang=enm}}
# {{lb|enm|law|rare}} An [[legal]] action in order to collect a money owed to one.

